 ## Introduction
 
-This guide describes how to set up two-way synchronization between OpenLDAP and OpenDJ. Changes made in OpenLDAP will be reflected in OpenDJ, and vice versa.
+[Read this section in the documentation](https://doc.openidentityplatform.org/openidm/how-to/configuring-openidm-for-synchronization-between-openldap-and-opendj#configuring-openidm-for-synchronization-between-openldap-and-opendj-introduction).
 
 ## OpenIDM Setup
 
-OpenIDM deployment is described in [documentation](https://doc.openidentityplatform.org/openidm/install-guide/). It is assumed that OpenIDM is already installed and ready to be configured.
+[Read this section in the documentation](https://doc.openidentityplatform.org/openidm/how-to/configuring-openidm-for-synchronization-between-openldap-and-opendj#configuring-openidm-for-synchronization-between-openldap-and-opendj-openidm-setup).
 
 ## Data Sources Setup
 
-### OpenLDAP Setup
-
-If you do not already have OpenLDAP installed, install it as described in [documentation](https://www.openldap.org/software/release/install.html). Or you can use the [Docker](https://hub.docker.com/r/bitnami/openldap/) image. This is the approach we will use in this article.
-
-Download the test data file [openldap-data.ldif](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/OpenIdentityPlatform/OpenIDM/files/openidm-openldap-dj/openldap-data.ldif) from GitHub and place it in the `./ldifs` directory that will be used to mount it in the 
+[Read this section in the documentation](https://doc.openidentityplatform.org/openidm/how-to/configuring-openidm-for-synchronization-between-openldap-and-opendj#configuring-openidm-for-synchronization-between-openldap-and-opendj-data-sources-setup).
 
+### OpenLDAP Setup
 
-```
- docker run --name openldap \
-  -p 2389:1389 -p 2636:1636 \
-  --env LDAP_ADMIN_USERNAME=admin \
-  --env LDAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=adminpassword \
-  --env LDAP_ROOT=dc=example,dc=com \
-  --env LDAP_ADMIN_DN=cn=admin,dc=example,dc=com \
-  -v ./ldifs:/ldifs \
-  bitnami/openldap:latest
-```
-
-After OpenLDAP starts, verify that the data is loaded by running the command
-
-```
-ldapsearch -x -H ldap://localhost:2389 -D "cn=admin,dc=example,dc=com" \
- -w adminpassword -b "dc=example,dc=com" "(objectClass=inetOrgPerson)" | grep dn
-dn: cn=user01,ou=users,dc=example,dc=com
-dn: cn=user02,ou=users,dc=example,dc=com
-```
-
-Download the OpenLDAP connection configuration file [provisioner.openicf-openldap.json](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/OpenIdentityPlatform/OpenIDM/files/openidm-openldap-dj/provisioner.openicf-openldap.json) from GitHub and copy it to the `conf` directory of OpenIDM.
-
-The file is already configured according to the OpenLDAP connection settings in the Docker container and requires no changes.
+[Read this section in the documentation](https://doc.openidentityplatform.org/openidm/how-to/configuring-openidm-for-synchronization-between-openldap-and-opendj#configuring-openidm-for-synchronization-between-openldap-and-opendj-openldap-setup).
 
